= The Moscow Olympics

The Soviet Union invaded Afghanistan over Christmas. President Carter wants the West to boycott the Moscow Olympics in protest. The British Olympic Association is independent of the government, and most of the athletes want to go.

- @boycott: Press the athletes to stay at home.
- @leave_it: Leave it to the sporting bodies.

@boycott
subtitle: The Americans are grateful. The athletes are not.
on-arrival: olympic_boycott = 1; us_relation += 6; right_dissent -= 2; thatcher_rating -= 1; c1_lib += 1

The government writes to every athlete urging them to stay away. The British Olympic Association refuses, and the team goes to Moscow anyway under the Olympic flag. Sebastian Coe and Steve Ovett win gold, and the government looks both heavy-handed and ignored.

@leave_it
subtitle: Washington notices.
on-arrival: us_relation -= 4; right_dissent += 2

The government condemns the invasion and leaves the Olympics to the sportsmen. The Americans conclude that their closest ally is not so close after all.

