= The Warrington By-election

Roy Jenkins, standing for the new Social Democratic Party, is fighting Warrington, one of the safest Labour seats in the North West. Our own candidate is struggling to be heard.

- @campaign_hard: Fight hard for our candidate.
- @save_effort: Save our effort for seats we can win.

@campaign_hard
subtitle: -1 resources.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent)

Labour holds the seat by fewer than two thousand votes. Jenkins calls it his first defeat in thirty years of politics and by far the greatest victory he has ever taken part in. We come a distant third.

@save_effort
subtitle: The Alliance gets a clearer run at Labour.
on-arrival: c1_lib += 1; lab_leader_rating -= 1

Labour holds the seat by fewer than two thousand votes. Our vote collapses and our candidate loses his deposit. The papers say the SDP is now the real opposition in the North.

