= The Royal Wedding

The Prince of Wales is to marry Lady Diana Spencer at St Paul's Cathedral. Three-quarters of a billion people around the world will watch on television. After a summer of riots, the country seems glad of something to celebrate.

- @holiday: Declare a national holiday.
- @no_holiday: Keep the country at work.

@holiday
subtitle: A small cost to the economy, and a lift in the national mood.
on-arrival: budget -= 0.3; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); de_con += 1*(1-dissent); thatcher_rating += 1 if con_in_government = 1

The wedding day is a bank holiday. Street parties fill the country, and for a day nobody talks about unemployment.

@no_holiday
subtitle: Business approves. Nobody else does.
on-arrival: ab_con += 1*(1-dissent); c2_con -= 1; thatcher_rating -= 1 if con_in_government = 1

Most people take the day off anyway. The papers call the government joyless.

