= Scargill

Arthur Scargill, the Yorkshire miners' leader who organised the flying pickets at Saltley Gate in 1972, has been elected President of the National Union of Mineworkers with seventy per cent of the vote. He has promised to fight every pit closure, by strike action if necessary.

- @prepare_miners: Prepare for a fight: more coal stocks, more oil-fired power.
- @keep_peace: Give the Coal Board money to keep the peace.

@prepare_miners
subtitle: -0.5 budget. Prepares for a miners' strike.
on-arrival: coal_stocks += 1 if coal_stocks < 3; budget -= 0.5; dry_dissent -= 2

The Energy Department quietly orders the power stations to build up their stocks and to burn more oil.

@keep_peace
subtitle: -1 budget. Industrial peace, for now.
on-arrival: budget -= 1; union_power += 2; strike_wave -= 1; dry_dissent += 3

The Coal Board's investment budget is raised, and closures are postponed. Scargill says the government has blinked.

