= The Rail Strike

The train drivers' union, ASLEF, is staging a series of strikes against British Rail's plan for flexible rostering, which would end the eight-hour day the drivers have worked since 1919. Commuters are stranded, and British Rail wants to know whether the government will back it.

- @back_br: Back British Rail: no deal without flexible rosters.
- @press_settle: Lean on British Rail to settle.

@back_br
subtitle: Union power falls. Commuters suffer for a while.
on-arrival: union_power -= 3; strike_wave += 1; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); economic_growth -= 0.1

British Rail threatens to sack every striking driver. The TUC refuses to back ASLEF, and the union gives in.

@press_settle
subtitle: -0.5 budget. The trains run; the dries despair.
on-arrival: union_power += 2; strike_wave -= 1; dry_dissent += 3; budget -= 0.5

British Rail drops the plan for now, and the drivers go back to work.

