= The Siberian Pipeline

President Reagan has banned American companies, and foreign companies using American technology, from supplying equipment for the Soviet gas pipeline to Western Europe. John Brown Engineering on the Clyde has a contract to build turbines for it. If it pulls out, hundreds of jobs go, and Washington will have told British firms whom they may trade with.

- @defy_us: Order British firms to honour their contracts.
- @comply: Go along with the Americans.

@defy_us
subtitle: Europe and the Clyde approve. Washington is not pleased.
on-arrival: pipeline_defied = 1; us_relation -= 6; europe_relation += 5; c2_con += 1*(1-dissent); scotland_con_bonus += 0.2

The Trade Secretary uses the Protection of Trading Interests Act to direct the firms to fulfil their contracts. You tell the Americans that a friend can disagree.

@comply
subtitle: Washington approves. The Clyde does not.
on-arrival: us_relation += 6; europe_relation -= 5; unemployment += 0.1; scotland_con_bonus -= 0.3

John Brown pulls out of the contract. Our European partners accuse us of doing Washington's bidding.

