= Greenham Common

Thirty thousand women link hands around the nine-mile perimeter fence of RAF Greenham Common, where American cruise missiles are due to arrive next year. The peace camp outside the main gate has been there for more than a year. CND's membership has passed a quarter of a million.

- @deploy: Cruise will be deployed on schedule.
- @delay: Signal a delay while the arms talks continue in Geneva.

@deploy
subtitle: Washington and the right approve. The peace movement is outraged.
on-arrival: cruise_deployed = 1; us_relation += 5; right_dissent -= 3; c1_lib += 1; de_lab += 1; wet_dissent += 1

The government says the missiles will arrive as planned. Ministers dismiss the peace camp as naive, and the camp grows.

@delay
subtitle: The Americans are furious. Moderate voters are relieved.
on-arrival: us_relation -= 8; right_dissent += 5; c1_con += 1*(1-dissent); lib_relation += 2

You tell the Commons that deployment depends on progress at Geneva. In Washington, the Pentagon briefs against you.

