= Bermondsey

In the by-election for Bermondsey, one of the safest Labour seats in London, the Liberal Simon Hughes defeats Labour's Peter Tatchell with a swing of 44 per cent, the largest in by-election history. Tatchell, a left-winger at first disowned by his own leader and then reinstated, faced one of the ugliest campaigns in modern British politics.

The lesson for us is simple: Labour's divisions can lose it even its safest seats.
